template:
RANDOM CODE AUDIT TASK

Workspace: {{workspace}}
Dedupe file: {{dedupe_file}}
Severity floor: {{severity_floor}}
Pipeline step: {{pipeline_step}}
Previous results: {{previous_results}}

Follow the skill exactly: randomly select a scope and a concern using the weighted `shuf` process, audit the selected code read-only for that concern, and write the RESULT artifact. Do not modify files. Treat spec/, intent/, and formal/ as authoritative when touched by the audit.

RESULT shape (write to the RESULT file at the workspace root):
{
  "signal": "pass|fix",
  "verdict": "PASS|FAIL",
  "summary": "one concise sentence naming scope + concern + finding count",
  "selection": {
    "scope_type": "global|focused|vertical",
    "scope_target": "directory/file or entire codebase",
    "vertical_path": "entry -> layer -> ... -> dependency (or empty)",
    "concern_type": "specific|generic",
    "concern": "the concern text only, no list index, no #N",
    "method": "the shuf commands used, including repicks"
  },
  "findings": [
    { "id": "F001", "severity": "CRITICAL|HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW|INFO",
      "path": "relative/file", "line": 1, "code": "snippet",
      "issue": "what is wrong and why it matters",
      "regression_test": "test that fails now and passes after fix, or N/A reason",
      "fix": "concrete remediation" }
  ],
  "stats": { "files_examined": 0 },
  "dedupe_fingerprint": "concern @ effective-scope"
}

verdict PASS = no actionable findings or only INFO. FAIL = one or more findings at LOW+. If no findings, findings must be an empty array.
